---
const { osuYears, michYears, seasonProfiles, provenance, matchupMethod } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="lab-shell" data-lab data-season-profiles={JSON.stringify(seasonProfiles)}>
  <header class="lab-header"><div><h1>RIVALRY LAB</h1><span>MODEL CARMEN-19.03</span></div><a class="lab-method-link" href="/rivalry-lab/about">METHOD &amp; SOURCES →</a></header>
  <nav class="lab-nav" aria-label="Rivalry Lab steps"><button data-screen="matchup" aria-current="step">1 · Matchup</button><button data-screen="tape">2 · Tape</button><button data-screen="pregame">3 · Pregame</button><button data-screen="game">4 · Game</button><button data-screen="postgame">5 · Postgame</button></nav>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="matchup"><h2><span class="osu">OHIO STATE <b data-osu-year>1995</b></span> AGAINST <span class="mich">MICHIGAN <b data-mich-year>2023</b></span>, ON NEUTRAL GROUND.</h2><p class="lede">Pick any available Ohio State or Michigan season. Both are translated into one neutral scoring era, then the game is simulated.</p><div class="selector-box"><label><b class="osu">OHIO STATE</b><select data-osu>{osuYears.map((year: number) => <option value={year} selected={year === 1995}>{year}</option>)}</select><small data-osu-facts>Loading season profile...</small></label><label><b class="mich">MICHIGAN</b><select data-mich>{michYears.map((year: number) => <option value={year} selected={year === 2023}>{year}</option>)}</select><small data-mich-facts>Loading season profile...</small></label></div><div class="lab-actions"><span>ERA NEUTRAL: each season is translated into a common scoring environment.</span><button class="primary" data-build>BUILD MATCHUP →</button></div></section>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="tape" hidden><div class="section-title"><h2>TALE OF THE TAPE</h2><span data-context></span></div><section class="season-profiles" aria-label="Selected season profiles" data-profiles></section><div class="lab-actions"><button class="secondary" data-screen="matchup">← SEASON SELECT</button><button class="primary" data-pregame>SIMULATE MATCHUP →</button></div></section>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="pregame" hidden><div class="section-title"><h2>PREGAME</h2><span data-pregame-context></span></div><div class="pregame-results"><section data-expected-score><p>EXPECTED SCORE <em>DERIVED</em></p><strong class="score" data-score>--</strong><small>Before any simulation</small></section><section data-expected-margin><p>EXPECTED MARGIN <em>DERIVED</em></p><strong data-margin>--</strong><small>Ohio State minus Michigan</small></section><section data-win-probability><p>WIN PROBABILITY <em>DERIVED</em></p><div class="probability"><div><strong class="osu" data-osu-prob>--%</strong><b>OHIO STATE</b></div><div><strong class="mich" data-mich-prob>--%</strong><b>MICHIGAN</b></div></div><div class="prob-bar"><i data-osu-bar></i><i data-mich-bar></i></div></section></div><section class="pregame-explanation"><div class="pregame-method" data-pregame-method><b>METHOD NOTE</b><p>Expected scores compare each offense with the opposing defense, add the overall-rating difference, and translate both sides to one neutral scoring environment. The expected margin is Ohio State's derived score minus Michigan's; win probability is the model's logistic transform of that margin.</p></div><div class="pregame-inputs" data-pregame-inputs><b>EXACT MODEL INPUTS <em>DERIVED</em></b><div data-input-list></div><p class="model-settings">Neutral baseline {matchupMethod.neutralPointsPerTeam.toFixed(1)} points per team · {matchupMethod.pointsPerStandardDeviation} points per standard deviation · advantage divisor {matchupMethod.matchupAdvantageDivisor} · probability margin scale {matchupMethod.winProbabilityMarginScale}</p></div></section><section class="drivers" data-pregame-drivers><div class="section-title"><h3>KEY DRIVERS</h3><span>DERIVED</span></div><div class="driver-grid"><article><b>Ohio State scoring edge</b><p data-osu-driver></p></article><article><b>Michigan scoring edge</b><p data-mich-driver></p></article></div></section><section class="provenance" data-testid="snapshot-provenance"><b>SOURCES &amp; PROVENANCE</b><p>Derived ratings: public Rivalry Lab product snapshot, generated {new Date(provenance.generatedAt).toISOString().slice(0, 10)}.</p><p>Snapshot: {provenance.ratingModelVersion} ratings · {provenance.eraModelVersion} era translation · {provenance.dataSnapshotVersion} data coverage.</p><p><a href="/rivalry-lab/about">READ THE METHOD</a></p></section><div class="lab-actions controls"><span>RUN SIMULATION</span><button data-run="1">PLAY ONE</button><button data-run="10">BEST OF 10</button><button data-run="100">SIM 100</button><button data-run="1000">SIM 1,000</button><button data-run="10000">SIM 10,000</button><label>SEED <input data-seed value="19952023" /></label></div><details data-chalk><summary>PREGAME CHALK TALK</summary><div data-chalk-panel></div></details></section>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="game" hidden><div class="game-score" data-game-score></div><section class="timeline" aria-label="Simulated drive timeline" data-timeline></section><div class="game-grid"><article data-turning></article><article data-game-stats></article></div><div class="lab-actions"><button class="secondary" data-rerun>RUN AGAIN WITH NEW SEED</button><button class="primary" data-postgame>VIEW POSTGAME →</button></div></section>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="postgame" hidden><div class="section-title"><h2>POSTGAME</h2><span data-series-context></span></div><div class="post-tabs" role="tablist"><button role="tab" data-tab="summary">Summary</button><button role="tab" data-tab="stats">Stats</button><button role="tab" data-tab="chalk">Chalk Talk</button></div><section data-post-panel></section><div class="lab-actions"><button class="secondary" data-screen="game">← SINGLE GAME</button><button class="secondary" data-screen="matchup">NEW MATCHUP</button></div></section>
  <footer>Rivalry Lab uses historical season data. Simulated games are model-generated, not historical results. Not affiliated with either university.</footer>
</section>
<script>
   type TeamId = 'ohio-state' | 'michigan';
   type SeasonProfile = { observed: { conference: string | null; division: string | null; coach: string | null; finalApRank: number | null; cfbdPostseasonRank: number | null; pointsPerGame: number | null; pointsAllowedPerGame: number | null }; derived: { overallRank: number | null; offenseRank: number | null; defenseRank: number | null; scheduleStrengthRank: number | null; ratedTeams: number | null }; confidence: { score: number | null; reasons: string[] } };
     type ProfileEntry = { teamId: TeamId; season: number; wins: number; losses: number; ties: number; crossEra: { overall: number; offense: number; defense: number }; profile: SeasonProfile | null };
    type MatchupResponse = { matchup: { neutralPointsPerTeam: number; ohioState: { expectedScore: number; winProbability: number; scoreAdvantage: number }; michigan: { expectedScore: number; winProbability: number; scoreAdvantage: number }; expectedMargin: number } };
   const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-lab]')!; const select = <T extends HTMLElement>(selector: string) => root.querySelector<T>(selector)!;
   const profiles = JSON.parse(root.dataset.seasonProfiles ?? '[]') as ProfileEntry[];
   let matchup: MatchupResponse['matchup']; let lastResult: any; let count = 1;
   const state = () => ({ osuYear: Number(select<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-osu]').value), michYear: Number(select<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-mich]').value), seed: select<HTMLInputElement>('[data-seed]').value });
   const track = (event: string, properties: Record<string, string | number>) => (window as Window & { gtag?: (...args: unknown[]) => void }).gtag?.('event', event, properties);
    async function getMatchup() { const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); const response = await fetch(`/api/matchup?osuYear=${osuYear}&michYear=${michYear}`); const payload = await response.json(); if (!response.ok) throw new Error(payload.error); matchup = payload.matchup; select('[data-osu-year]').textContent = String(osuYear); select('[data-mich-year]').textContent = String(michYear); const selectorSummary=(teamId:TeamId,year:number)=>{const entry=profiles.find((item)=>item.teamId===teamId&&item.season===year);if(!entry)return 'Profile not available in current source coverage.';const ap=entry.profile?.observed.finalApRank;const coach=entry.profile?.observed.coach??'Coach not available in current source coverage.';return `${entry.wins}-${entry.losses}${entry.ties?`-${entry.ties}`:''} · ${ap===null||ap===undefined?'Final AP rank not available in current source coverage.':`Final AP #${ap}`} · ${coach}`}; select('[data-osu-facts]').textContent=selectorSummary('ohio-state',osuYear); select('[data-mich-facts]').textContent=selectorSummary('michigan',michYear); const context = `${osuYear} OHIO STATE × ${michYear} MICHIGAN · ERA NEUTRAL`; select('[data-context]').textContent = context; select('[data-pregame-context]').textContent = context; renderTape(); renderPregame(); }
  function show(screen: string) { root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-view]').forEach((view) => view.hidden = view.dataset.view !== screen); root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.lab-nav button').forEach((button) => button.setAttribute('aria-current', button.dataset.screen === screen ? 'step' : 'false')); }
  const percentage = (value: number) => `${Math.round(value * 100)}%`;
   function rankLabel(rank: number | null, ratedTeams: number | null) { return rank === null ? 'UNRANKED' : `NO. ${rank}${ratedTeams === null ? '' : ` OF ${ratedTeams}`}`; }
   function profileCard(teamId: TeamId, season: number, teamName: string, color: string) { const profile = profiles.find((entry) => entry.teamId === teamId && entry.season === season)?.profile; if (!profile) return `<article class="season-profile ${color}" data-testid="season-profile-${teamId}"><header><b>${teamName} · ${season}</b><em>PROFILE UNAVAILABLE</em></header><p>This public snapshot has no observed or derived profile for this season.</p></article>`; const { observed, derived, confidence } = profile; const conference = [observed.conference, observed.division].filter(Boolean).join(' · ') || 'Conference not reported'; return `<article class="season-profile ${color}" data-testid="season-profile-${teamId}"><header><b>${teamName} · ${season}</b><em>SEASON PROFILE</em></header><p class="profile-record">${conference} · ${observed.coach ?? 'Coach not reported'}</p><div class="profile-facts"><span><small>OBSERVED SCORING</small><strong>${observed.pointsPerGame === null ? 'NOT REPORTED' : `${observed.pointsPerGame.toFixed(1)} PPG`}</strong><i>${observed.pointsAllowedPerGame === null ? 'Points allowed not reported' : `${observed.pointsAllowedPerGame.toFixed(1)} allowed per game`}</i></span><span><small>OBSERVED FINAL AP</small><strong>${observed.finalApRank === null ? 'UNRANKED' : `NO. ${observed.finalApRank}`}</strong><i>${observed.cfbdPostseasonRank === null ? 'CFBD postseason rank unavailable' : `CFBD postseason: No. ${observed.cfbdPostseasonRank}`}</i></span></div><div class="profile-ranks"><small>DERIVED SRS RANKINGS</small><span>OVERALL <b>${rankLabel(derived.overallRank, derived.ratedTeams)}</b></span><span>OFFENSE <b>${rankLabel(derived.offenseRank, derived.ratedTeams)}</b></span><span>DEFENSE <b>${rankLabel(derived.defenseRank, derived.ratedTeams)}</b></span><span>SCHEDULE <b>${rankLabel(derived.scheduleStrengthRank, derived.ratedTeams)}</b></span></div><p class="profile-confidence"><b>SNAPSHOT CONFIDENCE ${confidence.score === null ? 'NOT SCORED' : `${confidence.score}%`}</b>${confidence.reasons.length ? ` · ${confidence.reasons[0]}` : ''}</p></article>`; }
    function renderProfiles() { const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); select('[data-profiles]').innerHTML = `<div class="profile-grid">${profileCard('ohio-state', osuYear, 'OHIO STATE', 'osu')}${profileCard('michigan', michYear, 'MICHIGAN', 'mich')}</div>`; }
    function renderTape() { renderProfiles(); }
   function renderPregame() { const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); const osu = profiles.find((entry) => entry.teamId === 'ohio-state' && entry.season === osuYear)!; const mich = profiles.find((entry) => entry.teamId === 'michigan' && entry.season === michYear)!; select('[data-osu-prob]').textContent = percentage(matchup.ohioState.winProbability); select('[data-mich-prob]').textContent = percentage(matchup.michigan.winProbability); (select<HTMLElement>('[data-osu-bar]')).style.width = percentage(matchup.ohioState.winProbability); (select<HTMLElement>('[data-mich-bar]')).style.width = percentage(matchup.michigan.winProbability); select('[data-score]').innerHTML = `<span class="mich">${Math.round(matchup.michigan.expectedScore)} MICH</span> – <span class="osu">${Math.round(matchup.ohioState.expectedScore)} OSU</span>`; select('[data-margin]').textContent = `${matchup.expectedMargin >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${matchup.expectedMargin.toFixed(1)} OSU`; select('[data-osu-driver]').textContent = `${matchup.ohioState.scoreAdvantage.toFixed(1)} translated points above the neutral baseline.`; select('[data-mich-driver]').textContent = `${matchup.michigan.scoreAdvantage.toFixed(1)} translated points above the neutral baseline.`; select('[data-input-list]').innerHTML = [['Ohio State offense rating', osu.crossEra.offense, 'osu'], ['Michigan defense rating', mich.crossEra.defense, 'mich'], ['Ohio State overall rating', osu.crossEra.overall, 'osu'], ['Michigan offense rating', mich.crossEra.offense, 'mich'], ['Ohio State defense rating', osu.crossEra.defense, 'osu'], ['Michigan overall rating', mich.crossEra.overall, 'mich']].map(([label, value, color]) => `<span><small>${String(label).toUpperCase()}</small><strong class="${color}">${Number(value).toFixed(3)}</strong></span>`).join(''); }
    async function simulate() { count = 1; const response = await fetch('/api/simulate', { method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify({ ...state(), count }) }); const payload = await response.json(); if (!response.ok) throw new Error(payload.error); lastResult = payload.result; const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); track('rivalry_lab_simulation_run', { osu_season: osuYear, michigan_season: michYear, simulation_count: count }); renderGame(lastResult); show('game'); }
   function renderGame(game: any) { select('[data-game-score]').innerHTML = `<div><b class="mich">MICHIGAN</b><strong>${game.michigan.points}</strong></div><span>FINAL<br><small>SIMULATED</small></span><div><b class="osu">OHIO STATE</b><strong>${game.ohioState.points}</strong></div>`; select('[data-timeline]').innerHTML = game.drives.map((drive: any, index: number) => `<i title="Q${drive.quarter} · ${drive.outcome}" class="${drive.teamId === 'michigan' ? 'mich-bg' : 'osu-bg'}" style="animation-delay:${index * 40}ms">${drive.outcome}</i>`).join(''); select('[data-game-stats]').innerHTML = `<b>SIMULATED TEAM STATS</b><p><span>Ohio State</span> ${game.ohioState.possessions} possessions · ${game.ohioState.turnovers} turnovers</p><p><span>Michigan</span> ${game.michigan.possessions} possessions · ${game.michigan.turnovers} turnovers</p>`; }
    root.addEventListener('click', async (event) => { const target = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('button'); if (!target) return; try { if (target.dataset.screen) show(target.dataset.screen); if (target.matches('[data-build]')) { await getMatchup(); const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); track('rivalry_lab_matchup_built', { osu_season: osuYear, michigan_season: michYear, era_mode: 'neutral' }); show('tape'); } if (target.matches('[data-pregame]')) { await getMatchup(); show('pregame'); } if (target.matches('[data-run="1"]')) await simulate(); } catch (error) { alert(error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Unable to run Rivalry Lab'); } });
   select('[data-osu]').addEventListener('change', () => void getMatchup()); select('[data-mich]').addEventListener('change', () => void getMatchup()); select<HTMLDetailsElement>('[data-chalk]').addEventListener('toggle', async (event) => { if (!(event.currentTarget as HTMLDetailsElement).open || !matchup) return; const response = await fetch('/api/chalk-talk', { method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify({ matchup, simulation: count === 1 ? lastResult : undefined }) }); const payload = await response.json(); const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); track('rivalry_lab_chalk_talk_opened', { osu_season: osuYear, michigan_season: michYear, simulation_count: count }); select('[data-chalk-panel]').innerHTML = payload.panel.map((item: any) => `<article><b>${item.role}</b><p><em>${item.evidenceType}:</em> ${item.text}</p></article>`).join(''); });
  void getMatchup();
</script>

<script>
  const pregameScreen = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-view="pregame"]');
  const playOne = pregameScreen?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-run="1"]');
  const seed = pregameScreen?.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-seed]');
  const controls = playOne?.closest<HTMLElement>('.lab-actions');

  if (pregameScreen && playOne && controls) {
    const play = document.createElement('section');
    play.className = 'pregame-play';
    play.dataset.pregamePlay = '';
    play.innerHTML = '<p>Pick this matchup, then play one simulated game. The score, drive list, and team stats show what happened in this one seeded game.</p>';
    playOne.classList.add('play-one');
    play.append(playOne);
    const seedLabel = seed?.closest('label');
    if (seedLabel) play.append(seedLabel);
    else if (seed) play.append(seed);
    pregameScreen.querySelector('.pregame-results')?.before(play);
    controls.remove();
  }

  document.querySelector('[data-turning]')?.remove();
  document.querySelector('[data-view="game"] .lab-actions')?.remove();
  document.querySelector('[data-view="postgame"]')?.remove();
  document.querySelector('.lab-nav [data-screen="postgame"]')?.remove();
  document.querySelector('[data-chalk]')?.remove();
</script>

<script>
  const coverageLab = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-lab]');
  const coveragePregame = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-view="pregame"]');
  const coverageGame = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-view="game"]');

  async function renderSimulationCoverage() {
    if (!coverageLab || !coveragePregame) return;
    const osuYear = coverageLab.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-osu]')?.value;
    const michYear = coverageLab.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-mich]')?.value;
    if (!osuYear || !michYear) return;
    const response = await fetch(`/api/matchup?osuYear=${osuYear}&michYear=${michYear}`);
    if (!response.ok) return;
    const { simulationCoverage, usedInputs } = await response.json() as { simulationCoverage: 'box-score-enhanced' | 'score-and-schedule'; usedInputs: { possessionsPerGame?: { ohioState: number; michigan: number }; turnoversPerGame?: { ohioState: number; michigan: number } } };
    const coverageLabel = simulationCoverage === 'box-score-enhanced' ? 'ENRICHED' : 'SCORE-SCHEDULE';
    const coverage = simulationCoverage === 'box-score-enhanced'
      ? 'Historical possession and turnover context is active because both selected seasons have enrichment coverage.'
      : 'Score and schedule context is active. Possession and turnover context stays off unless both selected seasons have enrichment coverage.';
    let pregameContext = coveragePregame.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-simulation-coverage]');
    if (!pregameContext) {
      pregameContext = document.createElement('aside');
      pregameContext.dataset.simulationCoverage = '';
      pregameContext.className = 'simulation-coverage';
      coveragePregame.querySelector('.pregame-results')?.after(pregameContext);
    }
    pregameContext.innerHTML = `<b>SIMULATION COVERAGE · ${coverageLabel}</b><p>${coverage}</p>`;
    if (!coverageGame) return;
    let gameContext = coverageGame.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-game-coverage]');
    if (!gameContext) {
      gameContext = document.createElement('p');
      gameContext.dataset.gameCoverage = '';
      gameContext.className = 'simulation-game-context';
      coverageGame.querySelector('[data-game-score]')?.before(gameContext);
    }
    gameContext.textContent = `SIMULATION COVERAGE · ${coverageLabel}`;
  }

  new MutationObserver(() => {
    if (coveragePregame && !coveragePregame.hidden || coverageGame && !coverageGame.hidden) void renderSimulationCoverage();
  }).observe(coverageLab!, { attributes: true, subtree: true, attributeFilter: ['hidden'] });
  coverageLab?.querySelectorAll('select').forEach((input) => input.addEventListener('change', () => void renderSimulationCoverage()));
</script>

<script>
  const lab = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-lab]');
  let restoringHistory = false;
  const applyScreen = (screen: string) => {
    lab?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-view]').forEach((view) => {
      view.hidden = view.dataset.view !== screen;
    });
  };
  const requestedScreen = window.location.hash.slice(1);
  if (lab && lab.querySelector(`[data-view="${requestedScreen}"]`)) applyScreen(requestedScreen);
  else history.replaceState({ screen: 'matchup' }, '', '#matchup');
  window.addEventListener('popstate', () => {
    const screen = window.location.hash.slice(1) || 'matchup';
    restoringHistory = true;
    applyScreen(screen);
    window.setTimeout(() => { restoringHistory = false; }, 0);
  });
  new MutationObserver(() => {
    if (restoringHistory || !lab) return;
    const screen = lab.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-view]:not([hidden])')?.dataset.view;
    if (screen && window.location.hash !== `#${screen}`) history.pushState({ screen }, '', `#${screen}`);
  }).observe(lab!, { attributes: true, subtree: true, attributeFilter: ['hidden'] });
</script>

<script>
  const pregame = document.querySelector('[data-view="pregame"]');
  const margin = pregame?.querySelector('[data-margin]');
  const marginNote = pregame?.querySelector('[data-expected-margin] small');
  const method = pregame?.querySelector('[data-pregame-method]');
  const inputs = pregame?.querySelector('[data-pregame-inputs]');

  if (method) method.innerHTML = '<b>WHAT THIS MEANS</b><p>These numbers estimate a neutral-field matchup before the simulation adds game-to-game swings.</p>';
  if (inputs) {
    const heading = inputs.querySelector('b');
    const settings = inputs.querySelector('.model-settings');
    if (heading) heading.innerHTML = 'MATCHUP INPUTS <em>DERIVED</em>';
    if (settings) settings.textContent = 'Each team is compared with its own season before the model sets a common scoring baseline.';
  }
  const updateMarginNote = () => {
    if (!marginNote || !margin) return;
    const value = Number(margin.textContent?.replace(/[^0-9.-]/g, ''));
    marginNote.textContent = value === 0 ? 'Even matchup' : value > 0 ? 'Ohio State by expected margin' : 'Michigan by expected margin';
  };
  new MutationObserver(updateMarginNote).observe(margin ?? document.body, { childList: true, characterData: true, subtree: true });
  updateMarginNote();
</script>

<style is:global>
    .lab-header { display:flex;align-items:end;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px; }.lab-method-link,.lab-nav a { color:#111;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline 3px #bb0000;text-underline-offset:6px;white-space:nowrap; }.lab-nav a { padding:0 0 4px; }
    .pregame-play { display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;margin:20px 0;padding:18px 20px;background:#111;color:#fff; }.pregame-play p { max-width:620px;margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.4; }.pregame-play .play-one { min-width:180px;padding:16px 24px;font-size:18px; }.pregame-play label { display:grid;gap:5px;color:#fff;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.06em; }.pregame-play input { max-width:150px;font:16px 'Archivo Black'; }
     .game-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; }.simulation-coverage,.simulation-game-context { margin:18px 0 0;padding:13px 15px;border-left:5px solid #111;background:#f2f3f5; }.simulation-coverage b,.simulation-game-context { font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.06em; }.simulation-coverage p { margin:6px 0;color:#363a41;font-size:14px;line-height:1.4; }.simulation-coverage small { color:#6b717c;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.04em; }
